<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Meo people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Meos are a Muslim community of the Mewat region, in parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Mostly farmers, they converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in stages between about the 12th and 17th centuries but long kept many customs shared with their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> neighbours. Many lived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Alwar and Bharatpur, where they suffered violence and expulsion during Partition in 1947.</p></div>
